 ## Overview
-Hemisphere Illumination is a local shading model for volume rendering that simulates diffuse reflection from a virtual hemisphere light source to provide directional illumination cues in volume projections [S1, unofficial]. It enhances the perception of shape and spatial relationships by weighting volume points based on their orientation relative to a light direction, effectively treating the volume as a collection of diffusely reflecting surfaces [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard volume rendering which often lacks explicit shading cues, this method integrates radiance over a hemisphere, providing more accurate shadowing and illumination than simple directional lights, though it remains a local approximation without global occlusion [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Frequency Domain Directional Shading](852-frequency-domain-directional-shading.md) by using the gradient magnitude as the normal vector and computing the first moment of the spectrum.
