 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Zero Padding:** To avoid aliasing in the frequency domain, the input volume may need to be zero-padded. Increasing the volume width by a factor of $k^2$ (surrounding data with a margin of zeros of width $N(k^2-1)/2$) increases per-view processing time by $k^2$, memory by $k^3$, and preprocessing time by $k^2$ [S2, unofficial].
-- **Orientation Field:** The accuracy of the shading depends on the quality of the orientation field $N$. If $N$ is not accurately computed, the shading cues will be incorrect [S2, unofficial].
-- **No Occlusion:** The method does not account for occlusion between volume elements. Shading effects enhance shape perception but do not provide accurate shadows from other parts of the volume [S1, unofficial].
